# Normalise line endings in the repository, check out native on each platform.
#
# ⚑ WORTH HAVING FROM COMMIT ONE. Merging upstream into the server tree was nearly a
# 1000-file conflict because one side had been normalised to LF and the other had not, with
# no .gitattributes to reconcile them. Setting this now costs nothing; adding it after the
# fact rewrites every file.
* text=auto

# Scripts whose line endings are load-bearing
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Binaries - never touch these
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.db   binary
*.dll  binary
*.lib  binary
*.exe  binary
*.pdb  binary
*.zip  binary
*.sip  binary
*.tfc  binary
*.upk  binary

# The generated lookup tables are large and machine-written; a diff of them helps nobody.
# ⛔ SCOPED TO data/ ON PURPOSE. A bare "*.json -diff" would also silence launchSettings.json,
# the runtimeconfig files and every other project JSON, which are exactly the ones worth
# reading in a diff.
data/Costumes.json  -diff
data/Effects.json   -diff
